# tools/al/ales_scrub_witness.rish -- the scrub window, a small movable read dragged across a stereo master (ALES19).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus - the creative suite) - waymark ALES - rung ALES19.
# Design read: active-designing/20260814-fill-ales19-lotus-scrub.md
# Stands on: lotus/stereo_transport.rye (ALES15) -- the read head and read_block reused whole (a scrub read is a seek-then-read off
# that one head); lotus/stereo_meter.rye (ALES17) -- the StereoMeter reused whole for the level under the drag; lotus/pan.rye
# (ALES10) -- the StereoClip whose two channels share one length; lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2) -- the Clip and its max_clip bound.
#
# lotus/scrub.rye gives a keeper the gesture they edit by most: a short, fixed-length window they slide by hand across a stereo
# master. The crux: a scrub window read at position p returns EXACTLY the master's samples [p, p+n) in both channels, so dragging a
# scrub of length L across the master in steps of L TILES it -- the windows concatenate back to each channel byte-for-byte, the
# last window honestly short and a window at the end empty. Composing ALES17, metering a scrub window equals metering that master
# slice directly. The selftest proves: tiling at L of 1, 2, 3, 5; an arbitrary positioned read; meter_window equals a direct read;
# nudge clamps at both edges; a rendered center pan scrubs 0.707 per side (700); scrubbing and metering mutate neither channel; the
# edges refuse BadWindow / PastEnd / BadBlock by name. Purely local -- no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no meter.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_scrub_witness.rish

say "ales-scrub: Language EN — ALES19 gives a keeper a small fixed-length window they DRAG across a stereo master: a seek-then-read off the one ALES15 head, the editing gesture play and loop never offered."
say "ales-scrub: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: a scrub read at position p IS the master's own slice [p, p+n), so dragging the window in steps of its length tiles the master back byte-for-byte."
say "ales-scrub: Lens TAME — ALES15's read_block and ALES17's StereoMeter reused whole (no new copy path, no new arithmetic); the window length is bounded at make (≤ max_scrub_window ≤ the meter bound, so meter_window cannot overflow); nudge carries the signed drag in i64 and clamps to [0, len]; read-only, mutating neither channel; siloed to lotus/, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no meter, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/scrub"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/scrub.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-scrub: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/scrub.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-scrub: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-scrub: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-scrub' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-scrub: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-scrub line"

say "ales-scrub: GREEN — a scrub window dragged across a stereo master reads the master's own slice at every position, tiling it back byte-for-byte, its level metered true under the drag. With play, loop, and scrub all stereo and metered, the read side offers a keeper the three gestures they edit by. The next Lotus rung can offer the choice of pan/crossfade law on the scrub's read, name a markers track a scrub snaps to, or (a module seam) a punch region tying playback back to the Mikrophone's capture."
